                    "It should be 'The dogs barking'"
                ],
                "answer": 0,
                "explain": "The subject and verb must agree. 'dogs' is plural (more than one), so it takes the plain verb 'bark'. You add the -s to the verb only when the subject is a single thing: 'The dog barks'.",
                "rule": "A singular subject takes the -s verb; a plural subject takes the plain verb.",
                "principle": "Subject and verb must agree in number.",
                "canonical_solution": [
                    "'dogs' is plural",
                    "Plural subjects use the plain verb",
                    "So 'dogs bark', not 'dogs barks'",
